      '- ORIGINAL vs hybrid at the start of a demo: belt rocks drawn 784 vs 411. Roaming asteroids within 30,000 of the player: 262-280 vs 3-4. Nearest roaming asteroid 18,308 vs 29,444. Nearest small cluster about 5,000 vs 8,000+. In ORIGINAL at t=40 s the demo had flown to within 706 of a cluster.',
      '- Already fixed: with `asteroids: original` belt rocks skip the overhaul\'s angular cull, impostor tier and aerial fade in `updateDistanceCulling` and are culled by range; their materials are `toneMapped = false` with `HY_ROCK_ALBEDO` so they read as lit faceted rocks.',
      '- BLACK HOLES GREW: a standard core is now radius 900 (it was 36), its disc reaches 5.6 radii and the black-hole warp fires at 2.5 radii. ORIGINAL puts a core\'s belt 1,600-2,600 from the hole — now INSIDE the disc and the warp zone. The scale package (merged before you started) spaces large bodies by one rule in radii and was told about the belts; check what it did with them before you move anything.',
