      'Ben, verbatim (2026-10-11): "The demo player needs to clear the SOL system and then use a gravitational slingshot to get to Sagittarius A before proceeding with Nebula missions and clearing other black hole galaxies."',
      'Today the demo (js/autopilot.js, `window.demoPilot`, closure state `ap`, phases dispatched in `update()` → `switch (ap.phase)`) runs its own showcase: fight at Sol under a budget (HY_DEMO: 6 kills or 75 s — `_solBudgetOut` / `_solBudgetLeave` / the goPhase gate on \'combat\'/\'bossEngage\' in Sol), then `warpToNebulaCluster` → `coastToNebulaCluster` → `orbitNebulaPlanet`, `followDiscoveryPath`, `gotoBlackHoleGalaxy`, `bossEngage`, `fightBorg`, … The CAMPAIGN (js/progression.js, `progression: campaign`, `window.__campaign` { state, phases, advance(), mission, galaxy, guide, tether }) already runs in demo mode (briefings, guide lines, grants); the demo is exempt from its gravity tether and from the nebula guards (`guardTick`: `if (!c || isDemo()) return;`).',
      '',
      '## Build: a campaign director inside the demo',
      'When `window.__campaign` exists (and `HYBRID.is(\'progression\',\'campaign\')`), the demo follows the campaign state instead of the showcase sequence. Keep the showcase as the fallback when there is no campaign (`?hy=progression:overhaul`). Map each state to what the pilot does, reusing the existing phases and `navigateTo(pos, opts)` (the closed-loop controller: orient/thrust/jump/warp/brake):',
