      'NOTE: Ben\'s live messages go to the integrator, not to you — if one is relayed to you mid-run, record it in your report and keep doing THIS package.',
      'Ben, verbatim (2026-10-11): "we want to keep both versions of the player ship as options, but use the new ship for now. The thrusters, gun, and charge locations will needs some adjusting to match the new model."',
      'The new ship is `models/XT-7small.glb` (default since build 20261012i — see "ROUND 5" above for how it is baked; the stock hull `Player.glb` must keep working unchanged with `?hy=playerModel:Player`, and the wingmen always use the stock hull). Three effect families are anchored to the hull and all three were tuned to Player.glb:',
      '1. THRUSTERS — `createThrusterGlowsForModel(model)` in js/camera-system.js (~line 1126): two fixed model-local nozzle points (-0.022, 0, -0.125) / (0.022, 0, -0.125) with cones of radius 0.01 / 0.015, in the model\'s local frame (the root is scaled 96x by the game). Also the engine-bloom sprites / streak of `thrusters: overhaul` (grep `_ebState`, `engine-bloom`, `_installEngineBloom` in js/game-controls.js and js/visual-flair.js) — find where THEY take their position.',
      '2. GUNS — `getPlayerWingGuns()` + `_hyShipLocalBox()` + `_HY_GUN` {SPREAD 0.85, DOWN 0.10, FWD 0.75} in js/game-controls.js (~line 12824-12900): the laser origins, muzzle flashes and (via it) the charge glow are derived as fractions of the hull\'s own local bounding box. Read its header comment: it is the one source of truth, first person included.',
