      'On the XT-7 the fixed nozzle points sit inside the hull or beside it, the box fractions put the bolts off the real gun barrels, and the charge glow floats. Look at the XT-7 from every side first: `~/Desktop/InterstellarSlingshot-models/XT-7small/XT-7small-{left,right,top,bottom,front,back,iso}.png` (its raw nose is -X = the "left" view; in game the bake turns that to +Z). Identify the engine nozzles (how many, where) and the gun barrels / cannon muzzles (where on the wings or nose) and where a charge-up should visibly gather (the intake / nose / between the guns).',
      '',
      '## Build',
      '1. A PER-HULL ANCHOR TABLE `HY_HULL_POINTS` (window + a const in js/game-controls.js next to _HY_GUN): keyed by model name (`Player`, `XT-7small`, default = `Player`), in the hull\'s LOCAL frame as FRACTIONS of its local box (x: -1..1 of half-width, y: -1..1 of half-height, z: -1..1 of half-length, nose = +1) so they survive any scale: `thrusters: [{x,y,z, r}]` (nozzle points + cone radius as a fraction of hull width), `guns: [{x,y,z}]` (2 or more muzzles), `charge: {x,y,z, r}`. Measure the XT-7\'s numbers FROM ITS GEOMETRY: in a headless page (or a node script parsing the GLB — buffer views are plain float32 POSITION accessors) take the baked, in-game geometry (`modelCache.player` after load, geometry already baked to +Z nose), find the rear-most vertex clusters (nozzle rims: vertices within ~6% of min z, clustered by x/y), the forward-most protrusions at the wings or under the nose (barrels), and the hull\'s centreline for the charge point; confirm against the images. Put the numbers in the table with a comment saying how they were measured.',
      '2. ROUTE all three families through the table: `createThrusterGlowsForModel` reads the table for the current hull (the wingmen pass the stock hull → `Player` entry → EXACTLY today\'s numbers, so wingmen are unchanged), the engine-bloom sprites/streak the same; `getPlayerWingGuns` uses the table\'s guns when the hull has an entry (keep the box-fraction fallback for unknown hulls); the charge glow uses `charge`. Cone size and glow scale follow the hull\'s width so the XT-7\'s nozzles get plumes that fit them (the XT-7 is scaled to Player.glb\'s longest dimension, so its proportions differ).',
