      '## Build `titleScreen: launch` (new value; the three AG sketches stay selectable; `original` stays the default until Ben approves)',
      '1. THE SCENE = EARTH AT DAWN, FROM THE PAD. Layered: a real dawn sky gradient (deep violet zenith → teal → a gold band at the horizon, stars fading out toward the glow), thin drifting cloud bands, the eclipsed sun rising over the first ~8 s, the beat-line range as the stylised terrain (dawn palette: violet far rows, cyan middle, gold near — as in the mockup), and the PLAYER SHIP (the XT-7 — `models/XT-7small.glb` rendered live in a small WebGL canvas, as AG\'s poster did, OR a pre-rendered sprite from the turnarounds if the live canvas costs more than 2 ms/frame) sitting on the pad / hovering low at the right third, nav lights blinking and a faint idle thruster glow (reuse the look of package AE\'s hull lights). Slow parallax: the camera drifts ±2° over ~12 s; the range scrolls very slowly; reduced-motion (`prefers-reduced-motion`) disables the drift and glitch. No tear-bar glitch on the title except once at the logo reveal.',
